{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might","id":1329866,"title":"Charms of Underwhelming Might","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-08-08T04:24:49-07:00","id":1329866,"title":"Charms of Underwhelming Might","content":"Exalted Charms tend to be powerful as a rule, but every now and then there's a Charm that makes you go &quot;why would I ever buy this?&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you want to ask fellow players what good a Charm is because you can't figure it out yourself, if you want advice on buffing a Charm you think is underpowered, or if you just want to vent about Charms you think are terrible, this thread is for you!<br /> <br /> <br /> So I'll open with a question :<br /> <br /> Is the Lore Charm <b>Unstoppable Magnus Approach</b> worth getting at all? The Charm lets you pay 5 motes and 10 initiative to gain 1 temporary Willpower (with an explicit clause that you can't extend a fight artificially to farm Willpower). That seems like a terrible trade, especially for an Essence 5 Solar Charm with 10 pre-requisites (compare with <i>Spirit-Tempering Practice</i>, an Essence 3 Integrity Charm that gets you 1 willpower for 4 motes once per scene). Or is there something I'm not seeing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T04:51:35-07:00","id":1329870,"title":"","content":"I actually think Spirit-Tempering Practice is OP.<br /> <br /> Can Unstoppable Magnus be used out of combat? Otherwise, I can only see it used near the end of a combat when your Dawn friend is about to kill the last enemy and you're 2 range bands away with nothing much to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-08-2019, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T05:07:15-07:00","id":1329873,"title":"","content":"RAW the Charm description implies it can only be used in combat.<br /> <br /> I agree that Spirit-Tempering Practice is probably OP, although even without it as a comparison Unstoppable Magnus Approach still feels lackluster.<br /> <br /> It feels like the Charm is designed in a way where it only shines when used as a farming tool, which is explicitly prohibited. Like, by definition, if you're not allowed to accumulate more ini than you need to win a fight in order to use this Charm, then you will never have enough ini to use it except when the fight is already a bygone conclusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 08-08-2019, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T07:38:09-07:00","id":1329887,"title":"","content":"I could see it being used as a desperate grab. Plenty of other charms cost willpower, so a character could be running dangerously low thanks to other expenditures. Or if a character had been really liberal with Willpower for successes and then a nasty throw-down hit seemingly out of left field. Sorcery reimburses the Shaping willpower once the spell is cast, but you need enough gas in the tank to get the ball rolling.<br /> <br /> Granted, these are instances where I could see the benefit of &quot;oh shit!&quot; willpower grabs, rather than an explanation of how it's more powerful than it appears","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T08:25:38-07:00","id":1329894,"title":"","content":"I'll say that the Charms of 3rd Edition seem to suffer from this idea of either &quot;this is a highly-specialized trick; hopefully it's worth it!&quot; or &quot;this is a very broad power; good purchase!&quot; I'm getting a little uneasy familiarizing myself with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5706-zeal","name":"Zeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T08:53:07-07:00","id":1329902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1329894#post1329894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll say that the Charms of 3rd Edition seem to suffer from this idea of either &quot;this is a highly-specialized trick; hopefully it's worth it!&quot; or &quot;this is a very broad power; good purchase!&quot; I'm getting a little uneasy familiarizing myself with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This tends to happen with some of the Twilightish abilities (Bureaucracy, Craft, Integrity, Lore, Linguistics). Combat and Social trees are mostly pretty good in my experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T09:34:48-07:00","id":1329907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might#post1329866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Lore Charm <b>Unstoppable Magnus Approach</b> worth getting at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't think it is. In addition to the issues of cost you've already noted, it's pretty flavorless - just <i>why </i>is peerless mastery of Lore and enormous spiritual power (Lore 5, Essence 5 prereqs) required for this effect? Honestly, I think it would be better as an Integrity charm (and there's already an Integrity charm, Spirit-Tempering Practice, that lets you convert motes to WP). <br /> <br /> If I was rebuilding the charm, and had to keep it in Lore, here's how I'd do it:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Unstoppable Magnus Approach</b></span><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m, 10i; <b>Mins: </b>Lore 5, Essence 5<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Perilous<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene.<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Incalculable Flowing Mind, Surging Inner Fire<br /> The puissance of the Lawgiver's mind is so great that it grants her similar prowess on the battlefield. With dizzying intellect, she assess every possible fact and condition that might affect the course of battle, and cooly applies this knowledge to her own defense and offense. <br /> <br /> For the charm's duration, against any enemy who the Solar's educational background or specialties would apply, she may calculate her Evasion defense using [(Wits + Lore)/2, round up] - armor mobility penalty, rather than the typical (Dexterity + Dodge). Lore-based Evasion can be enhanced by the Lore Excellency. Any time she successfully avoids an attack in this matter, the proof of her mental superiority bolsters the Lawgiver, allowing her to roll her (current temporary Willpower) and gain initiative equal to her successes.<br /> <br /> The Copper Spider's knowledge can also be used offensively. She may make various gambits that exploit facts rather than her own combat skill to produce their effects. This can duplicate the effect of any gambit that the Solar can justify with information covered by her educational background. For instance, she might, if her educational background included human physiology, point out that a warrior's long exertions must surely have made his hand extremely sweaty, and his tendency to make wide swings would put considerable centrifugal force on his weapon - successfully completing a disarm gambit as it slipped out of his grasp. To achieve such a gambit, the Lawgiver rolls (Wits + Lore) in a <b>decisive</b> attack against her foe, who suffers a penalty to his Defense equal to the difference between his Wits and the Lawgiver's Wits, if his is lower. If the Solar hits, she rolls her initiative against the gambit's difficulty, as normal. Such gambits count as introductions of facts (Exalted 3rd Edition, pp. 237-238) for charms that enhance or otherwise affect that, but don't count against the normal once-per-scene limitation of such actions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T09:49:34-07:00","id":1329910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeal</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'll say that the Charms of 3rd Edition seem to suffer from this idea of either &quot;this is a highly-specialized trick; hopefully it's worth it!&quot; or &quot;this is a very broad power; good purchase!&quot; I'm getting a little uneasy familiarizing myself with them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While I'm not a huge fan of the Solar charmset, I wouldn't say that is a problem in a lot of it. I'd probably agree with Epitome that it's much more of an issue in Twilight abilities than others.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, in Lunars, I'm generally happy with the charmset; most of the charms are good but not overpowered.<br /> <br /> There's only one charm that I find too weak, one two of my players have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rugged Beast Endurance</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cost: 3m, 1wp; Type: Reflexive; Keywords: Protean; Duration: One day<br /> The... Lunar adapts to a particular environment... gaining temporary Survival and Resistance specialties in that clime. She ignores environmental penalties on rolls those specialties apply to.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, for 1wp, you get, say, Resistance (+1 vs freezing cold) and Survival (+1 vs freezing cold).<br /> You also ignore penalties on Resistance and Survival rolls caused by freezing cold.<br /> <br /> But environmental conditions normally don't apply penalties, they increase the difficulty. They only impose penalties when you're making opposed rolls, and Resistance and Survival aren't things you're normally going to be making opposed rolls on. For example, if the players are in a blizzard, they're going to make difficulty 2 Resistance rolls or something, not a difficulty 1 roll with a -2 penalty.<br /> <br /> So, 95% of the time, the charm is &quot;Pay 1wp, get +1 specialties on Resistance and Survival&quot;. Considering the charm is 8/10xp, and specialties cost 3xp each (or, hey, you could just buy more Resistance and Survival), I don't think it's worth spending 8/10xp and 1wp a day for a couple of specialties, even if you can apply them to different environments when you feel like it.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest, I've basically bumped up the charms' power by letting the Casteless character not make Resistance rolls for walking around the North in late winter without many clothes on (well, he's got a polar bear cloak now, but he still doesn't wear a shirt), because a)the charm is rubbish, and b)I can't be bothered to punish him for an aesthetic choice.<br /> <br /> I should say that the Protean benefit is okay (not amazing, but possibly you could do something good with Stamina charms) and the repurchase at Essence 2 is good. It's just the base charm that's weak.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Every other charm my players have seems good. It's just this one that seems weak.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-08-2019, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T10:16:51-07:00","id":1329917,"title":"","content":"So I typed out a post but it seemed way overly critical so I'm typing this instead whilst I work out how to say what I mean in a constructive way.<br /> <br /> But in short &quot;yes, I've noted several charms that I'd never take&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T11:38:59-07:00","id":1329941,"title":"","content":"Unimpeachable Discourse Technique. 3m to reroll 1s under extremely narrow circumstances. That <i>might</i> be decent as an Essence 1 DB Charm, but it\u2019s not, it\u2019s an Essence <i>2</i> Solar Charm. And half the best Socialize Charms are locked behind it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T12:41:16-07:00","id":1329954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1329941#post1329941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unimpeachable Discourse Technique. 3m to reroll 1s under extremely narrow circumstances. That <i>might</i> be decent as an Essence 1 DB Charm, but it\u2019s not, it\u2019s an Essence <i>2</i> Solar Charm. And half the best Socialize Charms are locked behind it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't Essence 2 Solar Charms on the whole somewhat narrower?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T14:10:43-07:00","id":1329968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1329954#post1329954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't Essence 2 Solar Charms on the whole somewhat narrower?</div> </div> </div> </div>Narrower =/= an Essence 1 dice trick but significantly worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T14:11:32-07:00","id":1329970,"title":"","content":"I don't really mind narrow charms that much; if they're useful for you, you'll buy them, if not, then you won't. Though if it just re-rolled 1s for 3m... I think that'd be quite a reasonable charm? (Very dull, but reasonable power-wise; and it's less irritating in its interactions with dice-caps than many of those kind of charms). The restriction on when you can use it seems like a needless nerf.<br /> The fact that much of the Socialise charm requires this charm you might rarely use seems a bit harsh though.<br /> <br /> But of course, the restriction is one that I think is probably not supposed to be a big restriction to the sort of characters Socialise is intended to be about.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T15:47:05-07:00","id":1329982,"title":"","content":"Talking about narrow I find the change from 2nd to 3rd solar mental defences extremely underwhelming you suddenly go from easy access to straightforward strong mental defences to extremely convoluted and narrow charms, that require multiple purchases to cover some of what used to be covered by 1 charm previously. This and solar crafting charms most of them look like they were written by a person who doesn\u2019t understand and hates crafting characters and the whole mess was written in a way to punish people who want to engage in it as means of putting people of it lunar crafting charms are way less offputting by comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12796,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","user":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","date":". 08-08-2019, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T16:30:42-07:00","id":1329990,"title":"","content":"I was interpreting that one as a way to stop a high-end social / psyche effect coming from somebody you'd really rather put your boot up.<br /> <br /> Not one that I'd buy, because we seem to be *pretty* good at bringing 2-dot stunts and WP bonuses when we need to, and there's also a low-level Integrity Charm that lets you buy off those costs. But that it was the intent. <br /> <br /> Maybe I'm missing something and if all the Solars were Unstoppable Magnoi the Usurpation would have broken differently?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T00:42:05-07:00","id":1330041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast of Bitter Oblivion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1329982#post1329982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talking about narrow I find the change from 2nd to 3rd solar mental defences extremely underwhelming you suddenly go from easy access to straightforward strong mental defences to extremely convoluted and narrow charms, that require multiple purchases to cover some of what used to be covered by 1 charm previously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Partly this is because social attacks are now that much weaker: they need to key off Intimacies. Basically you now have infinity purchases of 2E's Righteous Lion Defence for free. Layering further defences on top of that (and the right to just &quot;nope&quot; the most powerful social effects under the Red Rule) should be convoluted and narrowly applicable, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This and solar crafting charms most of them look like they were written by a person who doesn\u2019t understand and hates crafting characters and the whole mess was written in a way to punish people who want to engage in it as means of putting people of it lunar crafting charms are way less offputting by comparison. </div> </div> </div>I agree with this -- the Lunar charms are way less offputting. They are weaker though. If I were to play a crafter, I'd put up with the Solar charms -- the Lunar charms are better written, more interesting, less bloated... but the entire crafting system is written around Solar charms. I don't see how Lunars are successfully hitting Legendary TNs, or even completing Superior projects when they need to. But I haven't played a Lunar yet so maybe that's just my perception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T05:30:27-07:00","id":1330054,"title":"","content":"2nd ed's paradigm of players unleashing or suffering extremely powerful effects which became trivial to defend against if you bought the right charm ended up being quite dull. Weaker attacks/effects/influence rolls and weaker defences is actually more fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T09:59:37-07:00","id":1330072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330041#post1330041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with this -- the Lunar charms are way less offputting. They are weaker though. If I were to play a crafter, I'd put up with the Solar charms -- the Lunar charms are better written, more interesting, less bloated... but the entire crafting system is written around Solar charms. I don't see how Lunars are successfully hitting Legendary TNs, or even completing Superior projects when they need to. But I haven't played a Lunar yet so maybe that's just my perception.</div> </div> </div> </div>So my Lunar (who isn't really a crafter per-se, but has some craft, as she favours Intelligence) has... let me check... 1679 silver craft points and 108 gold points. I got that using one charm (Many-Phase Insights) and one month's work as a doctor (lots of crafting herbal medicines, then treating people with those medicines).<br /> <br /> Certainly, they're fine when it comes to getting craft points. Yes, my Lunar doesn't generate 8 gold points every single day out of nothing like my Solar crafter does, but she also doesn't have the vast amount of charms I bought to do that, before realising that you actually really don't need that many Craft points (I mean, I buy new Craft abilities with my gold points, but I've still got like 110, I don't have the time/opportunity to train a whole bunch of different craft skills).<br /> The Lunar craft-point charms start out better than the Solar ones, but don't go as far... which is fine, because as I said, you don't need as many as the pinnacle of the Solar tree gives you. And they also have a lot of charms that reduce the craft point cost.<br /> <br /> And the charm for getting free craft dots (buy one dot, get two) isn't as good as the Solar one (buy up to Essence crafts up to 5 with gold xp; I guess maybe that's expensive if you don't generate craft points out of your ass like me), but it's fine really. Buy two Crafts to 5, get two more for free at 5... that's probably enough for most characters, tbh.<br /> <br /> In terms of meeting successes...<br /> An Ess 2 Int 5, Craft 5 Lunar who stunts in, say, Strength 5, has 22 dice (that's min-maxed enough, I won't add a specialty).<br /> Wonder-Working Art x2 gives double 8s.<br /> <br /> So an average roll is going to be about 13 successes. Throw on a willpower and -4 for the difficulty is 10. So that makes level 2 and 3 artefacts very viable, but level 4s are pretty tricky. Level 5s are rather unfeasible.<br /> <br /> At Essence 5, and all the Craft charms, you could get 5 more dice, double 7s, and two extra terminus (though that does cost 12 white points, and unlike Solars you can't just buy them with gold points). That makes level 5s not a certain bet, but doable.<br /> <br /> Legendary artefacts though? No, I think that's going to be very, very difficult even for a maxed-out crafter. I'm okay with that though from a story perspective; Lunars just can't feasibly make the kind of incredible wonders that were forged in the First Age.<br /> And honestly, in 3rd ed, I've never seen anyone even attempt a Legendary Project, so not being able to do it wouldn't really put me off playing a Lunar crafter.<br /> <br /> What does put me off is the time taken to make artefacts.<br /> <br /> An Essence 1 and 2 Lunar both require 3 months to make a normal (lvl3) daiklaive.<br /> An Essence 2 Solar can buy Thousand-Forge Hands to reduce it to 1 month. An Essence 2 Lunar still requires 3 months.<br /> An Essence 3 Solar with TFH requires 3 weeks. An Essence 3 Lunar can buy Manifest-Miracle Forging, which reduces the time to 2 months.<br /> An Essence 4 Solar with TFH requires 2 weeks. An Essence 4 Lunar with MMF requires 2 months.<br /> An Essence 5 Lunar with TFH requires 1 week. An Essence 5 Lunar with MMF requires 2 months.<br /> <br /> Oh, and a suit of gunzota armour, lightning ballista, or other first-age artefact can't be reduced by Lunar craft charms.<br /> <br /> (A note on level 5 artefacts: an essence 2 Solar could do it in 4 months, while it takes 2 years for a Lunar. But I don't think many Essence 2 characters try to make lvl 5 artefacts. And after that they're fairly close; at Essence 3 it's 3 months for the Solar and 4 months for the Lunar.)<br /> <br /> I'm not saying Manifest-Miracle Forging is a badly designed charm. It's a fairly good charm; it covers creation and repair, and repair is much quicker (I think this is better than the seperate two Solar charms), it gives you a cost reduction (as I said, craft costs are pretty copable for Lunars).<br /> <br /> It does make sense to me that a)Lunars take longer to forge artefacts than Solars, and b)they're rubbish at making magitech.<br /> <br /> I just found that it was awkward to wait a few weeks to make an artefact if the game is fast-paced, and a few months is more so.<br /> <br /> Still, Lunars do have a)a charm that lets you used an unfinished artefact, and b)a charm that lets you start making... something, and just declare what it was at the end. So as soon as you've got some magical materials and 10 gold points, you could just start your inexplicable Lunar wonder, and then a few months later when someone gets a limb chopped off, reveal the prosthetic arm you happened to be working on all this time. Or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-09-2019, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T10:13:46-07:00","id":1330076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330072#post1330072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So my Lunar (who isn't really a crafter per-se, but has some craft, as she favours Intelligence) has... let me check... 1679 silver craft points and 108 gold points. I got that using one charm (Many-Phase Insights) and one month's work as a doctor (lots of crafting herbal medicines, then treating people with those medicines).<br /> <br /> Certainly, they're fine when it comes to getting craft points. Yes, my Lunar doesn't generate 8 gold points every single day out of nothing like my Solar crafter does, but she also doesn't have the vast amount of charms I bought to do that, before realising that you actually really don't need that many Craft points (I mean, I buy new Craft abilities with my gold points, but I've still got like 110, I don't have