months to make a normal (lvl3) daiklaive.<br /> An Essence 2 Solar can buy Thousand-Forge Hands to reduce it to 1 month. An Essence 2 Lunar still requires 3 months.<br /> An Essence 3 Solar with TFH requires 3 weeks. An Essence 3 Lunar can buy Manifest-Miracle Forging, which reduces the time to 2 months.<br /> An Essence 4 Solar with TFH requires 2 weeks. An Essence 4 Lunar with MMF requires 2 months.<br /> An Essence 5 Lunar with TFH requires 1 week. An Essence 5 Lunar with MMF requires 2 months.<br /> <br /> Oh, and a suit of gunzota armour, lightning ballista, or other first-age artefact can't be reduced by Lunar craft charms.<br /> <br /> (A note on level 5 artefacts: an essence 2 Solar could do it in 4 months, while it takes 2 years for a Lunar. But I don't think many Essence 2 characters try to make lvl 5 artefacts. And after that they're fairly close; at Essence 3 it's 3 months for the Solar and 4 months for the Lunar.)<br /> <br /> I'm not saying Manifest-Miracle Forging is a badly designed charm. It's a fairly good charm; it covers creation and repair, and repair is much quicker (I think this is better than the seperate two Solar charms), it gives you a cost reduction (as I said, craft costs are pretty copable for Lunars).<br /> <br /> It does make sense to me that a)Lunars take longer to forge artefacts than Solars, and b)they're rubbish at making magitech.<br /> <br /> I just found that it was awkward to wait a few weeks to make an artefact if the game is fast-paced, and a few months is more so.<br /> <br /> Still, Lunars do have a)a charm that lets you used an unfinished artefact, and b)a charm that lets you start making... something, and just declare what it was at the end. So as soon as you've got some magical materials and 10 gold points, you could just start your inexplicable Lunar wonder, and then a few months later when someone gets a limb chopped off, reveal the prosthetic arm you happened to be working on all this time. Or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wall of text crits you for 10 000 dmg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T10:33:52-07:00","id":1330077,"title":"","content":"Says the man who just reposted that entire text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T10:47:01-07:00","id":1330081,"title":"","content":"<b>Phantom Conjuring Performance</b> - this Essence 2 charm has <b>zero</b> mechanical effect. It's just stunt fodder, and risky stunt fodder at that, as it's not good for anathema to advertise. You'd guess that having a solar effect that made a magical light show would give you even a one dice bonus to a performance reception, alas no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T10:53:25-07:00","id":1330082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330072#post1330072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So my Lunar [actual in-play example here] Or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for that brilliant, in depth run-down. +1 Like.<br /> <br /> My response is simply this: Supernal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T11:14:21-07:00","id":1330091,"title":"","content":"Duh! I didn't even think of that. I only ever play very high essence characters (not by choice, that's just the games I'm in), 4 or 5, so no-one thinks much about Supernal. I do run an Essence 1 Lunar game, but obviously again no-one thinks about Supernal. But yeah, that'd be a huge difference between an Essence 1 Solar and Essence 1 Lunar.<br /> <br /> Obviously in the game-world Lunars are much more likely to have Essence 3 than Solars are, but in your game all the PCs will have the same Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T11:15:18-07:00","id":1330092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330082#post1330082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for that brilliant, in depth run-down. +1 Like.<br /> <br /> My response is simply this: Supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>You gotta be a masochist to take supernal craft tho. It\u2019s like playing with one hand tied behind your back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T11:35:41-07:00","id":1330098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330081#post1330081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Phantom Conjuring Performance</b> - this Essence 2 charm has <b>zero</b> mechanical effect. It's just stunt fodder, and risky stunt fodder at that, as it's not good for anathema to advertise.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I acknowledge that the charm text doesn't make this clear at all, I'd argue that Phantom Conjuring Performance actually has decent mechanical benefits in that it basically eliminates penalties for not having various presentation material prepared. Want to teach a bunch of illiterate peasants how to perform the ritual to appease the storm god? Phantom Conjuring Performance lets you create visual images of people doing the dances and shaking the rattles in the appropriate way. Trying to explain a complex battle plan? PCP makes a little battlefield diagram for you, no need to scrounge for rocks and draw in the dust. Heck, we're gamers here, I think we can all relate to the situation where you're describing something complex and the people listening are having a hard time keeping up. Just imagine being able to create a battlemat and miniatures out of your mind and magic light! In short, Phantom Conjuring Performance will eliminate penalties in a lot of circumstances, and as long as the ST is willing to use it that way, it's worth the cost in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T11:42:26-07:00","id":1330100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast of Bitter Oblivion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330092#post1330092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You gotta be a masochist to take supernal craft tho. It\u2019s like playing with one hand tied behind your back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which only speaks to how borked the craft system is and how horribly bloated the Solar craft charms are. If you actually want to be able to craft, I don't see how you could possibly play without taking Craft Supernal.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330098#post1330098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I acknowledge that the charm text doesn't make this clear at all, I'd argue [...] in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're houseruling charms to say they do stuff the text doesn't say they do, then my assessment of charms changes dramatically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 08-09-2019, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T12:01:14-07:00","id":1330101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330100#post1330100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're houseruling charms to say they do stuff the text doesn't say they do, then my assessment of charms changes dramatically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Charms can provide benefits not listed explicitly in their description when it makes sense, that's not houseruling, that's just the ST doing their storytelling. It's like the Bureaucracy Charms that let you know the exact value or quality of an item. They don't provide an explicit dice bonus or penalty negation, but they're obviously gonna help with bargain rolls and rolls having to do with buying and selling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 08-09-2019, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T12:14:44-07:00","id":1330105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330098#post1330098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I acknowledge that the charm text doesn't make this clear at all, I'd argue that Phantom Conjuring Performance actually has decent mechanical benefits in that it basically eliminates penalties for not having various presentation material prepared. Want to teach a bunch of illiterate peasants how to perform the ritual to appease the storm god? Phantom Conjuring Performance lets you create visual images of people doing the dances and shaking the rattles in the appropriate way. Trying to explain a complex battle plan? PCP makes a little battlefield diagram for you, no need to scrounge for rocks and draw in the dust. Heck, we're gamers here, I think we can all relate to the situation where you're describing something complex and the people listening are having a hard time keeping up. Just imagine being able to create a battlemat and miniatures out of your mind and magic light! In short, Phantom Conjuring Performance will eliminate penalties in a lot of circumstances, and as long as the ST is willing to use it that way, it's worth the cost in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that neither of these examples (war and lore) are exactly performance. The Charm-text describes that it only activated when one of the two pre-requisites are in effect, and both prerequisites are <b>performance supplemental</b>. <br /> <br /> Not that I wouldn't simply let a character stunt way having the maps and the teaching materials. You don't need a Charm to handwave menial tedious preparation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T12:52:19-07:00","id":1330109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast of Bitter Oblivion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330092#post1330092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You gotta be a masochist to take supernal craft tho. It\u2019s like playing with one hand tied behind your back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having played a Solar Supernal Craft character? Not really. The difference is that for most Supernals, the great thing is being able to pick one branch of your Charm tree and jump to the top fast. For Craft, it's being able to start with a few key Essence 2 Charms.<br /> <br /> Though I don't particularly like that, because, well, Solar Craft is not good design (I'll contend the Craft system itself is fine, which is why DB and Lunar crafting don't see the same complaints).<br /> <br /> ---------------<br /> <br /> One of my personal favorite examples of Charms that are worthless? Ten Ox Meditation. I'd take PCP as a Charm that has a purely narrative result, than a Charm with mechanics that directly screw over what the Charm is supposed to do.<br /> <br /> The whole point of the Charm is to surge your Strength to lift something above your current Strength limits.<br /> <br /> So you make a strongman character with Strength 5, Athletics 5 (relevant specialty), and Mighty Thews 3 for a base 14 dice to feats of strength. So lifting anything in the Str 3 or Str 5 categories isn't too bad, and even at the top Excellencies alone should get you there (up to 24 dice and you need 9 successes at most).<br /> <br /> But you need to lift an elephant. Well now you need Strength 7, and to roll 10 successes. This is where TOM is supposed to shine. 24 dice to hit 10 successes... wait no, now it's 24 dice to hit 16 successes... which is not great odds... and I hope you weren't expecting to lift a tyrant lizard any time soon.<br /> <br /> The example from the books requires spending 17m, and an Essence 2 Charm into the mix, and it only has a ~2/3s odds of actually working despite all that.<br /> <br /> If you're not Athletics Supernal TOM is not going to work until you get higher Essence Charms... so why bother. If you are Athletics Supernal... just ignore it and get to Nine Aeon Thews which is better than TOM in every way save the WP cost (but hoping TOM works means you'd be spending WP on those rolls anyway)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T12:57:12-07:00","id":1330111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330100#post1330100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which only speaks to how borked the craft system is and how horribly bloated the Solar craft charms are. If you actually want to be able to craft, I don't see how you could possibly play without taking Craft Supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>While Solar Craft definitely does have more charms than it probably needs, I'd argue that a non-Supernal crafter is totally viable. There are 16 Essence 1 Solar Craft charms, but I can easily see taking just a few and still being quite useful. Offhand, I'd go for Tireless Workhorse Method, Arete-Shifting Prana, and Craftsman Needs No Tools. With those three, I'll have enough major project slots to work on even a 5-dot artifact if I want to try (or, more likely, be working on a 2- or 3-dot one, and have major slots left over to do other projects to generate gold points in the meantime. I'll also be able to shift my crafting dots to the skills I need to complete a project. And, of course, I'll be able to finish basic and major projects amazingly quickly, without tools.<br /> <br /> And with just those charms and the Craft Excellency, I'd have a better-than-average chance of finishing a 2-dot artifact, and at least a hope, assuming good rolls, of getting a 3-dot. And I'd be pretty incredibly useful for mundane crafting. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're houseruling charms to say they do stuff the text doesn't say they do, then my assessment of charms changes dramatically.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is houseruling Phantom Conjuring Performance. The charm says that while you're under the effects of one of its prerequisites, &quot;phantoms coalesce [...]and aid in illustrating [your] narrative.&quot; A &quot;narrative&quot; doesn't have to be a literal story - if I'm describing a battle strategy, my narrative is how I expect the battle to go. So PCP should help illustrate that. And imposing penalties for <i>not</i> having visual representations is simply an extension of the ST's general prerogative to assign appropriate modifiers for situations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T13:19:27-07:00","id":1330115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330105#post1330105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Note that neither of these examples (war and lore) are exactly performance. The Charm-text describes that it only activated when one of the two pre-requisites are in effect, and both prerequisites are <b>performance supplemental</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Coming up</i> with the strategy or lesson would be War or Lore. <i>Presenting</i> the material to others is Performance, though. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that I wouldn't simply let a character stunt way having the maps and the teaching materials. You don't need a Charm to handwave menial tedious preparation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, if there's time to prepare, it's not necessary. There's not always that time, though, and preparation materials can be dangerous too. If you have five minutes before your camp is overrun by a talon of Realm soldiers, and you've got a strategy to lay out to your lieutenants, PCP is going to help a lot. Or if you're trying to teach a bunch of peasants the true history of Creation in a town with a lot of Immaculate monks searching for proscribed literature, it's nice to not have to carry any.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T13:27:46-07:00","id":1330119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1329907#post1329907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really don't think it is. In addition to the issues of cost you've already noted, it's pretty flavorless - just <i>why </i>is peerless mastery of Lore and enormous spiritual power (Lore 5, Essence 5 prereqs) required for this effect? Honestly, I think it would be better as an Integrity charm (and there's already an Integrity charm, Spirit-Tempering Practice, that lets you convert motes to WP).<br /> <br /> If I was rebuilding the charm, and had to keep it in Lore, here's how I'd do it:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Unstoppable Magnus Approach</b></span><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m, 10i; <b>Mins: </b>Lore 5, Essence 5<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Perilous<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene.<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Incalculable Flowing Mind, Surging Inner Fire<br /> The puissance of the Lawgiver's mind is so great that it grants her similar prowess on the battlefield. With dizzying intellect, she assess every possible fact and condition that might affect the course of battle, and cooly applies this knowledge to her own defense and offense.<br /> <br /> For the charm's duration, against any enemy who the Solar's educational background or specialties would apply, she may calculate her Evasion defense using [(Wits + Lore)/2, round up] - armor mobility penalty, rather than the typical (Dexterity + Dodge). Lore-based Evasion can be enhanced by the Lore Excellency. Any time she successfully avoids an attack in this matter, the proof of her mental superiority bolsters the Lawgiver, allowing her to roll her (current temporary Willpower) and gain initiative equal to her successes.<br /> <br /> The Copper Spider's knowledge can also be used offensively. She may make various gambits that exploit facts rather than her own combat skill to produce their effects. This can duplicate the effect of any gambit that the Solar can justify with information covered by her educational background. For instance, she might, if her educational background included human physiology, point out that a warrior's long exertions must surely have made his hand extremely sweaty, and his tendency to make wide swings would put considerable centrifugal force on his weapon - successfully completing a disarm gambit as it slipped out of his grasp. To achieve such a gambit, the Lawgiver rolls (Wits + Lore) in a <b>decisive</b> attack against her foe, who suffers a penalty to his Defense equal to the difference between his Wits and the Lawgiver's Wits, if his is lower. If the Solar hits, she rolls her initiative against the gambit's difficulty, as normal. Such gambits count as introductions of facts (Exalted 3rd Edition, pp. 237-238) for charms that enhance or otherwise affect that, but don't count against the normal once-per-scene limitation of such actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that Charm a lot, although it would probably go at the end of the Introduce-a-fact tree rather than at the end of the give-motes-and-willpower-to-my-friends tree. If I remade the Charm I'd probably try something like this :<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Unstoppable Magnus Approach</b></span><br /> <b>Cost: </b>None <b>Mins: </b>Lore 5, Essence 5<br /> <b>Type: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Incalculable Flowing Mind, Surging Inner Fire<br /> Manipulating the flow of Essence on the battlefield, the Lawgiver is a force of nature beyond the reach of the enemy. So long as she has not declared an attack or gambit, her foes must pay willpower equal to (3 or all their remaining Willpower, minimum 1) before they can begin attacking her (further attacks by that enemy can be made without paying willpower). Once per fight, the Exalt can steal the paid willpower and spread it among herself and nearby allies (max 1wp gained per target, including the Exalt)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T13:40:31-07:00","id":1330122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330115#post1330115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Coming up</i> with the strategy or lesson would be War or Lore. <i>Presenting</i> the material to others is Performance, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, since we are going so deep into the splitting hair country, if it's improvised, the skill to be used is presence. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, if there's time to prepare, it's not necessary. There's not always that time, though, and preparation materials can be dangerous too. If you have five minutes before your camp is overrun by a talon of Realm soldiers, and you've got a strategy to lay out to your lieutenants, PCP is going to help a lot. Or if you're trying to teach a bunch of peasants the true history of Creation in a town with a lot of Immaculate monks searching for proscribed literature, it's nice to not have to carry any. </div> </div> </div>I would say, if you are going to teach a bunch of peasants, doing showy anathema presentations is a very bad way to go. <br /> <br /> It's a bad charm if you are going to invent some penalties you'd never consider otherwise just to justify its existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T13:43:37-07:00","id":1330124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330109#post1330109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having played a Solar Supernal Craft character? Not really. The difference is that for most Supernals, the great thing is being able to pick one branch of your Charm tree and jump to the top fast. For Craft, it's being able to start with a few key Essence 2 Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, I'd agree with that. Thousand-Forge Hands so you can make artefacts in a practical timespan, Supreme Perfection of Craft if you want a ton of craft points, and basically all the good power charms that actually make it feasible to make artefacts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll contend the Craft system itself is fine, which is why DB and Lunar crafting don't see the same complaints </div> </div> </div>Originally I thought the Craft system was terrible, but over time I've moved to the same view as you. I think Lunar and DB craft are fairly reasonable, though I haven't seen them used much in practice (I have seen Solar Craft used in practice, and I'm very much unimpressed).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of my personal favorite examples of Charms that are worthless? Ten Ox Meditation. </div> </div> </div>Oh man, I forgot how annoying that charm is.<br /> <br /> Luckily, it's not the prereq for anything, so you can just take all the other Feat-of-Strength charms and ignore it.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also remembered a second really weak charm from Lunars; Mountainous Spirit Expression.<br /> <br /> Towering Beast Form is a very expensive charm that gives you Legendary Size, free excellency dice, big damage, big soak, and some special attacks, and probably a few other merits too.<br /> <br /> Mountainous Spirit Expression is a very expensive charm that gives you Legendary Size. And that's it.<br /> You can turn into Mothra, but you're Mothra with Soak 1 and a lower damage pool than a human's fist. One of my players described it as turning into a giant balloon, you're so eminently poppable.<br /> <br /> It also requires Towering Beast Form, Strength 5 and Essence 2. It's an &quot;upgrade&quot; which is, 90% of the time, worse than the prereq charm.<br /> <br /> There are times you could do something clever with it; it's not a terrible choice for a DBT build. But it's certainly not a very good choice for other forms. Considering the massive cost (15m, 1wp, 4 motes a round), I'm not sure it's worth it just for Legendary Size.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still, Vance said it was on his list for a second look, so hopefully the final version will be improved.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Mountainous Spirit Expression, Rugged Beast Endurance...<br /> Tbh, 2 poor charms in the whole Lunar book seems pretty good to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T14:11:58-07:00","id":1330130,"title":"","content":"Unless I missed an errata or something, TOM is a speed bump for the quite desirable Triumph-Forged God-Body.<br /> <br /> You don't need it if you're planning to mostly stick to the feats of strength stuff, but permanent double 9s for all Athletics rolls is really tempting and the other prereqs are nice; and you'd want Monkey Leap Technique to snag Thunderbolt Attack Prana anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T15:10:29-07:00","id":1330142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330119#post1330119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like that Charm a lot, although it would probably go at the end of the Introduce-a-fact tree rather than at the end of the give-motes-and-willpower-to-my-friends tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point, yeah. I had forgotten where exactly Unstoppable Magnus Approach actually was. I guess I'd put a charm with the effect I wrote up above Truth Rendering Gaze, though I think I'd like to make up something else to go in between Truth-Rendering Gaze and that, just because the jump from Essence 2 to Essence 5 seems a bit high. Solar Lore could stand to have a few more fact-introduction charms anyway, I feel.<br /> <br /> If I remade the Charm I'd probably try something like this :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Unstoppable Magnus Approach</b></span><br /> <b>Cost: </b>None <b>Mins: </b>Lore 5, Essence 5<br /> <b>Type: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Incalculable Flowing Mind, Surging Inner Fire<br /> Manipulating the flow of Essence on the battlefield, the Lawgiver is a force of nature beyond the reach of the enemy. So long as she has not declared an attack or gambit, her foes must pay willpower equal to (3 or all their remaining Willpower, minimum 1) before they can begin attacking her (further attacks by that enemy can be made without paying willpower). Once per fight, the Exalt can steal the paid willpower and spread it among herself and nearby allies (max 1wp gained per target, including the Exalt)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this effect is unbalanced, but I don't think it feels very Lore-y. In fact, it's quite close to Majestic Radiant Presence, and feels more like a Presence charm. Here's another take on Unstoppable Magnus Approach that focuses on the Willpower-theft element.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Unstoppable Magnus Approach</b></span><br /> <b>Cost: </b>1m, 2i <b>Mins: </b>Lore 5, Essence 5<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Perilous<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Incalculable Flowing Mind, Surging Inner Fire<br /> The Copper Spider knows that mental effort is no mere abstraction, but is instead a real (if ephemeral) energy. Her command over the mysteries of the mind is so acute that she can feel when others use this energy, and benefit from it herself. Any time someone within Medium range of the Solar spends temporary willpower for any reason, she becomes aware of it automatically, and may activate this charm. If she does so, the other person still gains the benefit of the expended willpower, but it is not lost to the mental ether. Instead, the Lawgiver gains the temporary willpower herself. This may increase her willpower above her normal maximum, though any such excess gained through this charm vanishes at the end of the scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T15:39:03-07:00","id":1330148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330142#post1330142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think this effect is unbalanced, but I don't think it feels very Lore-y. In fact, it's quite close to Majestic Radiant Presence, and feels more like a Presence charm. Here's another take on Unstoppable Magnus Approach that focuses on the Willpower-theft element.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Unstoppable Magnus Approach</b></span><br /> <b>Cost: </b>1m, 2i <b>Mins: </b>Lore 5, Essence 5<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Perilous<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Incalculable Flowing Mind, Surging Inner Fire<br /> The Copper Spider knows that mental effort is no mere abstraction, but is instead a real (if ephemeral) energy. Her command over the mysteries of the mind is so acute that she can feel when others use this energy, and benefit from it herself. Any time someone within Medium range of the Solar spends temporary willpower for any reason, she becomes aware of it automatically, and may activate this charm. If she does so, the other person still gains the benefit of the expended willpower, but it is not lost to the mental ether. Instead, the Lawgiver gains the temporary willpower herself. This may increase her willpower above her normal maximum, though any such excess gained through this charm vanishes at the end of the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh dear. The synergy between this and Will-Bolstering Method means you can use this to triple your willpower pool... now that's an Essence 5 end-of-tree Solar Charm alright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T19:54:49-07:00","id":1330192,"title":"","content":"Threefold Magnetic Ardor costs 4 motes, and unless your Appearance is 4+ <i>more</i> than your target's Resolve, it's less efficient than just using your Presence Excellency.<br /> <br /> And if your Appearance really is that much higher than their Resolve, you probably don't need much help convincing them anyway.<br /> <br /> I guess TMA does have the slight advantage of working on Performance and Socialize rolls in addition to its native Presence. So it's slightly useful in the edge case where you don't even have the Excellency for one of those and you have to make a roll anyway. I really don't think that justifies it, though.<br /> <br /> Seeing as it's required for Awakened Carnal Demiurge, which some people actually do want, it would be nice if it were a little more useful. Maybe it should just be cheaper?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T00:36:46-07:00","id":1330217,"title":"","content":"Revolving-Hurricane-Force Defense...just...why are the pre-reqs for this aura water charms when it's an aura air charm. I've tried but haven't been able to figure out the reason for that one.<br /> <br /> Also, and I've even run tests and I'm still not sure how I feel about Shimmering Heat Mirage Tactic. Is it good? It seemed like it was okay when I tested it out but maybe I was just lucky? I still have no idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T01:58:34-07:00","id":1330222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330217#post1330217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Revolving-Hurricane-Force Defense...just...why are the pre-reqs for this aura water charms when it's an aura air charm. I've tried but haven't been able to figure out the reason for that one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that quite common?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T02:12:46-07:00","id":1330224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330222#post1330222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that quite common?</div> </div> </div> </div>*Bite my tongue.*<br /> *Bite my tongue.*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T03:40:06-07:00","id":1330230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast of Bitter Oblivion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1329982#post1329982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talking about narrow I find the change from 2nd to 3rd solar mental defences extremely underwhelming you suddenly go from easy access to straightforward strong mental defences to extremely convoluted and narrow charms, that require multiple purchases to cover some of what used to be covered by 1 charm previously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this about Psyche effects, or about the game no longer giving Solars a casual capacity to never be open to persuasion or manipulation by anybody else ever?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast of Bitter Oblivion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This and solar crafting charms most of them look like they were written by a person who doesn\u2019t understand and hates crafting characters and the whole mess was written in a way to punish people who want to engage in it as means of putting people of it</div> </div> </div> </div>How is that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T03:50:43-07:00","id":1330231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330081#post1330081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Phantom Conjuring Performance</b> - this Essence 2 charm has <b>zero</b> mechanical effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you're roleplaying, do you not picture the scene being played in your mind? Do characters not interact based on visual stimuli?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">risky stunt fodder at that, as it's not good for anathema to advertise.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wyld Hunt is an element of the setting that is designed to be applied flexibly, written as both dangerous when they turn up and built in with multiple justifications for why they can't always turn up.<br /> <br /> Being Anathema isn't right in Mahalanka.<br /> <br /> And one could perhaps use the unique vectors of performance provided by being able to accompany them with phantom images towards making being Anathema elsewhere less dangerous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T08:17:35-07:00","id":1330251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330230#post1330230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this about Psyche effects, or about the game no longer giving Solars a casual capacity to never be open to persuasion or manipulation by anybody else ever?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> How is that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don\u2019t worry about it, I wouldn\u2019t expect the person who doesn\u2019t play to understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12796,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","user":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","date":". 08-10-2019, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T08:31:15-07:00","id":1330255,"title":"","content":"That's kind of a dickish thing to say, can we try and be civil please.<br /> <br /> My experience playing 2nd ed is that a story-long perfect defence vs social influence is pretty dull.<br /> <br /> I'll also add that I quite like the anti-shaping defence, the way it works is much more fun than the 2nd ed version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-10-2019, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T08:36:38-07:00","id":1330256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330224#post1330224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Bite my tongue.*<br /> *Bite my tongue.*</div> </div> </div> </div>I realised I misread it; I was thinking that water charms are often prereqs for air charms, etc, which isn't such a big deal. <br /> I guess DrLoveMonkey's point is that they are aura-required,and I guess needing to buy a prereq that's literally impossible to combo is pretty annoying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T09:06:56-07:00","id":1330259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330256#post1330256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I realised I misread it; I was thinking that water charms are often prereqs for air charms, etc, which isn't such a big deal. <br /> I guess DrLoveMonkey's point is that they are aura-required,and I guess needing to buy a prereq that's literally impossible to combo is pretty annoying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's the main one. I just don't see a great reason why they couldn't have branched earlier down the tree rather than being placed after an earth/water/wood charm, then two water charms that are all aura keyworded. I think overall the design is solid, but that one baffles me a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T13:54:35-07:00","id":1330295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330256#post1330256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I realised I misread it; I was thinking that water charms are often prereqs for air charms, etc, which isn't such a big deal. <br /> I guess DrLoveMonkey's point is that they are aura-required,and I guess needing to buy a prereq that's literally impossible to combo is pretty annoying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I'm going the other way on this. Charms of different Aspects in the same cascade bugs the heck out of me.<br /> <br /> &quot;These charms are thematically linked, so they're prerequisites. But they're not thematically linked so they're different elements.&quot;<br /> <br /> And, you know, that covers basically all the DB charms. But it seems churlish to complain that basically the entire DB charmset is underwhelming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T14:22:00-07:00","id":1330298,"title":"","content":"I don't find it underwhelming so much as finickity, because of all the contrasting aura states and so on. Actually, there's quite a lot of powerful charms compared to 2nd ed, especially the signature charms, but they tend to be really awkward to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T14:40:37-07:00","id":1330301,"title":"","content":"Which is... kinda the point? The devs wanted the DB Charms to not just be &quot;Solar Charms, but worse,&quot; so the trade off is that it's a lot harder for them to go all out because their Charms take work to get going at their strongest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T15:39:22-07:00","id":1330308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330301#post1330301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is... kinda the point? The devs wanted the DB Charms to not just be &quot;Solar Charms, but worse,&quot; so the trade off is that it's a lot harder for them to go all out because their Charms take work to get going at their strongest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the goal was achieved, it's just some of the fun was sacrificed to get there.<br /> <br /> Ideally there could be a system where DBs can shine, but which doesn't rely on creating a labyrinth of unintuitive constraints for players to navigate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T15:52:58-07:00","id":1330309,"title":"","content":"Sure. But fun and underwhelming aren't really the same thing. Wyld Shaping Technique isn't underwhelming in what it can do (even if you need to invest in the upgrade Charms to really get a lot out of it), but the complexity of it is pretty high and cane easily turn people off since it's Charm that introduces its own custom sub-system to use.<br /> <br /> I think the DB Charms could have probably gone more Aura as a bonus instead of a requirement so more of the Charms are functional even if not full power if you're not in Aura, and you'd get less complaints about how the elements Charms are tagged as not working well for holding Aura. But I don't think the difficulty of holding Aura should been too heavily weighed into the value of the DB Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T16:05:51-07:00","id":1330311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330309#post1330309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. But fun and underwhelming aren't really the same thing. Wyld Shaping Technique isn't underwhelming in what it can do (even if you need to invest in the upgrade Charms to really get a lot out of it), but the complexity of it is pretty high and cane easily turn people off since it's Charm that introduces its own custom sub-system to use.<br /> <br /> I think the DB Charms could have probably gone more Aura as a bonus instead of a requirement so more of the Charms are functional even if not full power if you're not in Aura, and you'd get less complaints about how the elements Charms are tagged as not working well for holding Aura. But I don't think the difficulty of holding Aura should been too heavily weighed into the value of the DB Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, I think that a lot of the unfunness of Aura comes from the way it's designed as penalties and restrictions rather than as empowerment and bonuses. The mechanical result is the same, technically, but the difference in how it feels can be huge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T16:44:31-07:00","id":1330317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330311#post1330311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree, I think that a lot of the unfunness of Aura comes from the way it's designed as penalties and restrictions rather than as empowerment and bonuses. The mechanical result is the same, technically, but the difference in how it feels can be huge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, can you explain this a bit more? From what I\u2019ve seen and remember it\u2019s usually \u201ccharm does x, in aura it also does y.\u201d<br /> <br /> The aura effect in general I like, as I think it does do what it\u2019s supposed to, which is allow a bunch of cool powerful charms that can\u2019t be combined together into something more powerful than is appropriate. So you can\u2019t Swaying Grass Elusion while countering with Unassailable Body of Fire and redirecting the attack with Safety Among Enemies and stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T16:55:35-07:00","id":1330319,"title":"","content":"The 2 things I'm thinking of here are :<br /> <br /> -Aura Charms which can't be used at all without the right Aura<br /> -The way that your Aspect makes some Charms and Abilities intrinsically worse because of the way Bonfire anima interacts with Aura.<br /> <br /> One thing I like about Aura is what they did with Martial Arts. Expending Aura to remove the Terrestrial keywords feels empowering and creates new gameplay possibilities as you choose which of your Charms should get the big oomph.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T18:21:45-07:00","id":1330330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast of Bitter Oblivion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330251#post1330251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don\u2019t worry about it, I wouldn\u2019t expect the person who doesn\u2019t play to understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a person who plays the game weekly, I disagree on both the notions that Craft feels like it was made by people who hate crafters, and that playing the game is necessary to understand the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T18:44:37-07:00","id":1330334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330330#post1330330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a person who plays the game weekly, I disagree on both the notions that Craft feels like it was made by people who hate crafters, and that playing the game is necessary to understand the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you are entitled to your opinion I don\u2019t agree I don\u2019t think that seeing charms so to speak in a vacuum is the same as acquiring and experiencing them in play. There is nothing quite as demotivating for a player to slogging their way up the crafting tree where every charm other players get elsewhere meaningfully add to your legend where as your charms are soul suckingly punishing adding little to your experience on their own. Also I don\u2019t see sorcerers having to buy 3 different craft skills at 5 20 crafting charms grind crafting xp of 4 different colours buy project slots and rare magical materials to make working which has similar if not greater significance on gameplay if this isn\u2019t hate what is that then gross incompetence ? Crafting doesn\u2019t need to be easy it just shouldn\u2019t be mindnumbingly boring and overly complicated the way it is now and the worst crime its neither heroic or fulfilling . I\u2019d feel more epic and exalted playing a twilight accountant with bureaucracy charms with way less xp and time wasted feeling the pulse of the nation at your fingertips.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12796,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","user":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","date":". 08-10-2019, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T20:48:34-07:00","id":1330342,"title":"","content":"Solar crafters \u201cneed\u201d exactly three Charms (six counting prereqs): Sublime Transference, Thousand-Forge Hands, and Bright-Forging Prana. Anything more than that is for N/As or thinking orichalcum grows on trees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T23:25:55-07:00","id":1330350,"title":"","content":"Well, you don't even necessarily need Sublime Transference, though in practice for most people it makes a huge difference.<br /> Also, if you're Essence 3+, I actually think it's better to get Experiential Conjuring of the Void (I think? I'm away from the book now. The one that gives you a whole bunch of non-charm dice), as Bright-Forging Prana is 1/story.<br /> <br /> I've brought the point-generation charms with 2 characters, and found it a big trap. There's a lot of traps in the craft tree.*<br /> <br /> Although while that's true about the charms, Beast also mentioned having to buy multiple Abilities, which is quite frustrating.<br /> <br /> *But since this thread is supposed to be about individual charms that are weak, rather than opinions about a contraversial system generally, I'd like to talk about the Slots tree. Once you have the first charm (+Ess x2 major slots) there are several charms that are superfluous, all they do is save you a couple of silver points. But they're prereqs for some interesting charms, which is annoying.<br /> I forget the names, I'll check later.<br /> <br /> But I think it's notable that the writers didn't bother writing any slot charms for Lunars or DBs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T23:38:18-07:00","id":1330352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330317#post1330317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmm, can you explain this a bit more? From what I\u2019ve seen and remember it\u2019s usually \u201ccharm does x, in aura it also does y.\u201d<br /> <br /> The aura effect in general I like, as I think it does do what it\u2019s supposed to, which is allow a bunch of cool powerful charms that can\u2019t be combined together into something more powerful than is appropriate. So you can\u2019t Swaying Grass Elusion while countering with Unassailable Body of Fire and redirecting the attack with Safety Among Enemies and stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand why they had the idea, but I'd have preferred a simple rule of &quot;these charms can't be comboed&quot; to &quot;use an element charm on your turn, and then don't use any charms from different elements until the end of your turn, and after that as long as you don't use charms from other elements you can use this charm and that charm becomes more powerful&quot;.<br /> <br /> Basically, I find the way DBs go into Aura too finickity, rather than what happens in it.<br /> <br /> It may be fine for PCs, but when I'm running some DB NPCs vs a group of PCs there's already a lot to keep track of. So I ended up building the characters' combat suites entirely around how complex aura is; the fire swordsman who uses only fire charms, the air martial artist who doesn't bother, etc.<br /> <br /> Actually I asked my friend who runs a DB game how the players find it, he said one mechanically-minded guy uses it, one guy's character always has the same aura so it's fine, and the others don't buy any Aura charms because they can't get their heads around it, which he thinks is a pity as they're avoiding some of the most fun and powerful charms.<br /> <br /> But anyway, I agree with Heavy Arms; the issue here isn't individually underwhelming charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T07:12:03-07:00","id":1330380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330231#post1330231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When you're roleplaying, do you not picture the scene being played in your mind? Do characters not interact based on visual stimuli?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, visual stimuli is very important. However, this charm gives no bonuses to the associated performance roll. So, it either bypasses the rule system (&quot;0 success on the performance roll?! You still succeed!&quot;) or is meant to be in-system and completely underwhelming (&quot;2 success on the supplemented performance roll is still less than the public's resolve. No effect!&quot;). This Charm, like every other Charm, should have a system effect. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> The Wyld Hunt is an element of the setting that is designed to be applied flexibly, written as both dangerous when they turn up and built in with multiple justifications for why they can't always turn up.<br /> <br /> Being Anathema isn't right in Mahalanka. </div> </div> </div>But, it is still an existing menace in the setting, and fame as an Anathema is pretty much a bad idea. The point is, this is a point against the Charm, and there are no positives.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T09:16:24-07:00","id":1330393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330350#post1330350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*But since this thread is supposed to be about individual charms that are weak, rather than opinions about a contraversial system generally, I'd like to talk about the Slots tree. Once you have the first charm (+Ess x2 major slots) there are several charms that are superfluous, all they do is save you a couple of silver points. But they're prereqs for some interesting charms, which is annoying.<br /> I forget the names, I'll check later.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was Efficient Craftsman Technique. You've already got more Major slots than you need from the prereq; 8xp to reduce the cost of extra slots from 5 silver points to 3 is a complete waste.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T13:02:24-07:00","id":1330430,"title":"","content":"Efficient Craftsman Technique is kinda weird, because at low Essence, it's actually pretty handy; esp. if you're not investing a lot of Charms into Craft. But as your Essence goes up (boosting Tireless Workhorse Method), and you probably purchase some more Charms... you have a ton that make the savings from Efficient Craftsman Technique increasingly pointless. <br /> <br /> But this whole section of the Solar Craft tree is bloated to hell and back. It has a bunch of utility, which it then tends to make redundant rather than more useless later, but spread around far too much Charms (esp. repurchasing Dragon Soul Emergence and God-Forge Within... though wth does DSE give you 1 superior slot per purchase, while G-FW gives you 2 legendary slots?).<br /> <br /> Vice-Miracle Technique, Wonder-Forging Genius (because it's the only way you'll speed up a legendary project to see it happen in most games), and Dual Magnus Prana are pretty much all the Charms after Sublime Transference that aren't in need of some amount of work as they're all fairly bland/underwhelming in their own ways; esp. as a whole.<br /> <br /> You can make this so much more tolerable if Tireless Workhorse Method and Efficient Craftsman Technique had automatic upgrades at Essence 3 and 5 to apply to Superior and Legendary respectively (not necessarily word for word), ignore all the cxp generating effects and let the Momentum tree do that, salvage Summit-Piercing Touch and Unwinding Gyre Meditation as at least neat concepts, do something about Exegesis of the Distilled Form and Sun-Heart Tenacity so they're more flexible do the length of in-game time and aren't undercut by the need for decades to pass in-game for them to really be used, and clarify what Spirit-Stoking Elevation actually applies to. Though I'll acknowledge the white cxp to normal XP thing is a bit questionable as a mechanic; it isn't underwhelming though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-12T14:02:47-07:00","id":1330611,"title":"","content":"Btw I had the time of my life playing a Twilight non-Supernal crafter (I had like 3 Charms, basically the one to be fast, to change ability points, and the one to roll better) and it was a blast. So obviously my character wasn't (yet) the divine crafter brought to this world to create so many wonders they can't even be numbered, but I could still do some fun crafting.<br /> <br /> I really appreciated finding some little tasks to use my crafts during fight, social or emotionnal scenes, managing my crafting points to try to achieve greater works for my people. I totally get why it could become a real bother late game when you have so much points you don't even know what to do with them.<br /> <br /> My problem is a lot of the charms are indeed boring to buy. The first ones that give you sometimes 1 more silver experience per objective per charm, and 1 gold point when you trigger all objectives are really not interesting when you see what later charms awaits.<br /> <br /> Changing the subject from craft Charms, I believe a few Socialize Charms are really uninteresting, because they are mainly little dice tricks that let you save motes, and so I guess your anima burns less and you also have less fun :<br /> <br /> I believe the worst offender is Shadow Over Day, 1 mote for 1 guile, or 2 motes for 2 guile. It's not like &quot;your rate of guile becomes 1 guilde for 1 mote&quot;, it's literally you can have 1 guile and that's all. I don't think the 2motes version make up for this.<br /> <br /> In the same way, even if I guess for some of them it can be discussed, I would add : Umbral Eyes Focus (basically saving you 2 motes under specific circumstances), I guess Night Passes Over is not totally terrible as it reduces penalty, but not for the actual only penalties to Guilde described in the book, Deep-Eyed Soul Gazing when bought at essence 2 allows to you, under specific circumstances, save up 1 mote.<br /> <br /> I mean I know with this kind of reasoning I could be grumpy about much more Charms, but I find these specific ones, especially compared to fun Socialize Charms like Discretionnary Gesture or Mastery of Small Manners or Indecent Proposal Method, really boring<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-12T15:54:52-07:00","id":1330639,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve been having fun with Socialize Supernal. But to be fair, I haven\u2019t played with all the toys in the box yet - mostly because we\u2019ve been advancing so fast that I\u2019ve been acquiring Charms faster than I can use them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T08:28:07-07:00","id":1330751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast of Bitter Oblivion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330334#post1330334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Crafting doesn\u2019t need to be easy it just shouldn\u2019t be mindnumbingly boring and overly complicated the way it is now and the worst crime its neither heroic or fulfilling .</div> </div> </div> </div>That is weird... I find crafting pretty damned awesome, fulfilling and very entertaining... And that is without ever having crafted a single Artifact. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T08:51:40-07:00","id":1330754,"title":"","content":"I have a desire to do a crafter and I have not much interest in Artifacts. The Water Craft sig where you do a major project super fast is hella neat; the idea of just sort of swooshing out a thousand arrows or a bridge in the middle of a battle is way my deal.<br /> <br /> Re: Socialize, I get how Night Passes Over isn't terribly exciting, though I also see its value in slightly tightening up your Guile costs. Maybe it would be better-served if it weren't just that as its own Charm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8026,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","user":"Beans","date":". 08-13-2019, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T09:21:17-07:00","id":1330760,"title":"","content":"Or reduced the cost by more than just 2m for +2 or more. Like you could get +5 for 5 motes rather than 10.<br /> <br /> Though, honestly, if you're facing a lot of Read Intentions actions in a scene, I think getting +2 for 2 motes instead of 4 is okay for a starting charm. A lot of the social trees start with charms that are just &quot;have an excellency for cheaper&quot;. Not super awesome, but I'm not that bothered they're there.<br /> (Although I have found them a bit annoying because players often forget the way they interact with dice tricks, especially ones that add auto-successes. And sometimes players say &quot;I'm using Blah-Blah&quot;, the ST says &quot;what does that do&quot; and they're like &quot;oh, it adds blah, blah, blah&quot; and they could have just said &quot;it makes excellencies cheaper.&quot; Basically, I think it's not clear to less mechanically-minded players that what the charm does is just make excellencies cheaper.<br /> But these are not necessarily bad charms. A few are, because sometimes they're not actually cheaper than an excellency, but Night Passes Over isn't one of those, it's always saving you motes.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T09:29:14-07:00","id":1330764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330754#post1330754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a desire to do a crafter and I have not much interest in Artifacts. The Water Craft sig where you do a major project super fast is hella neat; the idea of just sort of swooshing out a thousand arrows or a bridge in the middle of a battle is way my deal.<br /> <br /> Re: Socialize, I get how Night Passes Over isn't terribly exciting, though I also see its value in slightly tightening up your Guile costs. Maybe it would be better-served if it weren't just that as its own Charm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I could see it being fusionned with some other Charms that let you save up motes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or reduced the cost by more than just 2m for +2 or more. Like you could get +5 for 5 motes rather than 10.<br /> <br /> Though, honestly, if you're facing a lot of Read Intentions actions in a scene, I think getting +2 for 2 motes instead of 4 is okay for a starting charm. A lot of the social trees start with charms that are just &quot;have an excellency for cheaper&quot;. Not super awesome, but I'm not that bothered they're there.<br /> (Although I have found them a bit annoying because players often forget the way they interact with dice tricks, especially ones that add auto-successes. And sometimes players say &quot;I'm using Blah-Blah&quot;, the ST says &quot;what does that do&quot; and they're like &quot;oh, it adds blah, blah, blah&quot; and they could have just said &quot;it makes excellencies cheaper.&quot; Basically, I think it's not clear to less mechanically-minded players that what the charm does is just make excellencies cheaper.<br /> But these are not necessarily bad charms. A few are, because sometimes they're not actually cheaper than an excellency, but Night Passes Over isn't one of those, it's always saving you motes.) </div> </div> </div>I think it would be acceptable if I didn't find 4 different Charms Essence in Essence 1 and 2 that basically let you sometimes save you 2 motes for 1 roll in some specific occasions. This topic is about underwhelming Charms, and when you compare this to any other correct Charm I don't see them competing with those Charms (namely those I gave like Mastery of Small Manners, Indecent Proposal Method, etc ...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T09:47:04-07:00","id":1330769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330764#post1330764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would be acceptable if I didn't find 4 different Charms Essence in Essence 1 and 2 that basically let you sometimes save you 2 motes for 1 roll in some specific occasions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was sceptical of this, so I checked, and you're right. There's Umbral Eyes Focus (way to specific), Preeminent Gala Knife (really good), and Deep-Eyed Soul Gazing (worth it at high Essence, I guess? At Essence 2 it's saving you a single mote under certain circumstances).<br /> <br /> I guess they're all saving you motes under different circumstances, but I can see your point about it being pretty dull.<br /> Shadow Over Day+Preeminent Gala Knife are actually a very good combo (basically, get +2 Guile for free), but the other two, meh. Luckily, Umbral Eyes Focus doesn't seem to be a prereq for anything, but Deep-Eyed Soul Gazing is a prereq for quite a lot of charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T09:50:59-07:00","id":1330770,"title":"","content":"All the &quot;make Excellencies cheaper&quot; charms are all underwhelming, unless they're scene long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T12:51:18-07:00","id":1330789,"title":"","content":"So, A DB thing that isn't about Aura! Naked Thief Style, what's the point?<br /> <br /> You already use Dexterity+Larceny to conceal things on your body. Such things, being small, are easy to hide already, so the only advantage seems to be...<br /> <br /> &quot;Characters cannot roll (Perception + Awareness) to contest this concealment unless they\u2019re within short range of the Exalt or use magic that extends the range of their senses. She may stack up to (Dexterity) uses of this Charm to conceal multiple items.&quot;<br /> <br /> Is that a problem that needs a solution? Do thieves usually have trouble with guards who can spot their concealed lockpicks from Medium range? Do they usually pass through checkpoints where the guards are barely within earshot of the people they're scrutinizing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T13:28:27-07:00","id":1330801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amayad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330789#post1330789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, A DB thing that isn't about Aura! Naked Thief Style, what's the point?<br /> <br /> You already use Dexterity+Larceny to conceal things on your body. Such things, being small, are easy to hide already, so the only advantage seems to be...<br /> <br /> &quot;Characters cannot roll (Perception + Awareness) to contest this concealment unless they\u2019re within short range of the Exalt or use magic that extends the range of their senses. She may stack up to (Dexterity) uses of this Charm to conceal multiple items.&quot;<br /> <br /> Is that a problem that needs a solution? Do thieves usually have trouble with guards who can spot their concealed lockpicks from Medium range? Do they usually pass through checkpoints where the guards are barely within earshot of the people they're scrutinizing?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd argue that the real benefit isn't the range of detection, it's the fact that it seems to allow an unpenalized roll no matter how you're dressed (handy when you're trying to slip thieves tools in while disguised as an exotic dancer, for instance), and what exactly counts as a &quot;small item you can hold in one hand&quot;. While &quot;anything you can lift with one hand&quot; is probably a bit too broad, I'd rule that it's larger than whatever can literally fit within your palm. A dagger, for instance, seems pretty reasonable to be concealed with this charm. <br /> <br /> All that said, it's still kind of anemic, I'd agree. I'd probably shorten the range things can detect the hidden items down to only close.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T13:56:28-07:00","id":1330809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1329870#post1329870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually think Spirit-Tempering Practice is OP.<br /> <br /> Can Unstoppable Magnus be used out of combat? Otherwise, I can only see it used near the end of a combat when your Dawn friend is about to kill the last enemy and you're 2 range bands away with nothing much to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I can see it as a method for when you already dominate in an encounter so you spend easy to replenish resources to get harder to replenish ones. But yeah it\u2019s hard to grock if it\u2019s worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T14:01:19-07:00","id":1330812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330801#post1330801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd argue that the real benefit isn't the range of detection, it's the fact that it seems to allow an unpenalized roll no matter how you're dressed (handy when you're trying to slip thieves tools in while disguised as an exotic dancer, for instance), and what exactly counts as a &quot;small item you can hold in one hand&quot;. While &quot;anything you can lift with one hand&quot; is probably a bit too broad, I'd rule that it's larger than whatever can literally fit within your palm. A dagger, for instance, seems pretty reasonable to be concealed with this charm.<br /> <br /> All that said, it's still kind of anemic, I'd agree. I'd probably shorten the range things can detect the hidden items down to only close.</div> </div> </div> </div>To add to this, it's also stackable up to 5 times. So you can hide things on your person I'd say no larger than <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/474x/2d/44/0f/2d440f8bb90c4cad30c19f5fe9a9afe8--thieves-tools-lockpick.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> without penalty. Then when you get into the back room of the party you pull out your thieves tools, disguise kit, short daiklave, glass flask of acid and hand winch and get to work. For people within short range they can attempt a roll, but it's not automatic. It's not super strong but it's an Essence 1 DB charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T14:18:22-07:00","id":1330817,"title":"","content":"I had to write an entire thread about how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308338-effectively-using-raging-fire-dragon-spirit\">Effectively use Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit</a>.<br /> <br /> It's not a Charm I can see any non-Fire Aspect ever bothering to buy, and then only Fire Aspects who rely on Fire Dragon Style, since Fire Aspects with Melee could get Harnessed Firestorm Assault instead.<br /> <br /> Brawl's Fire Signature Charm, Erupting Fury Barrage, doesn't seem worth the effort of a Fire Aspect investing so much into Brawl, and I don't see any other Aspect bothering to grab that Charm because of the difficulty of a brawler generating the necessary Fire Aura.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-14T05:39:23-07:00","id":1330914,"title":"","content":"[Edit]<br /> <br /> My reading of this Charm was completely wrong as <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1331064#post1331064\">Vance confirms</a>.<br /> <br /> You can ignore everything I've written below:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330812#post1330812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To add to this, it's also stackable up to 5 times. So you can hide things on your person I'd say no larger than <a href=\"http://&quot;https://i.pinimg.com/474x/2d/44/0f/2d440f8bb90c4cad30c19f5fe9a9afe8--thieves-tools-lockpick.jpg&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> without penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>In normal, everyday attire, what penalty would you apply?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then when you get into the back room of the party you pull out your thieves tools, disguise kit, short daiklave, glass flask of acid and hand winch and get to work. For people within short range they can attempt a roll, but it's not automatic. It's not super strong but it's an Essence 1 DB charm. </div> </div> </div>I expect at least this much strength from a charm: <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=c_1FJGCAPxo\" target=\"_blank\">https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=c_1FJGCAPxo</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 08-15-2019, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-14T09:53:38-07:00","id":1330941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1329910#post1329910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> While I'm not a huge fan of the Solar charmset, I wouldn't say that is a problem in a lot of it. I'd probably agree with Epitome that it's much more of an issue in Twilight abilities than others.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, in Lunars, I'm generally happy with the charmset; most of the charms are good but not overpowered.<br /> <br /> There's only one charm that I find too weak, one two of my players have.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, for 1wp, you get, say, Resistance (+1 vs freezing cold) and Survival (+1 vs freezing cold).<br /> You also ignore penalties on Resistance and Survival rolls caused by freezing cold.<br /> <br /> But environmental conditions normally don't apply penalties, they increase the difficulty. They only impose penalties when you're making opposed rolls, and Resistance and Survival aren't things you're normally going to be making opposed rolls on. For example, if the players are in a blizzard, they're going to make difficulty 2 Resistance rolls or something, not a difficulty 1 roll with a -2 penalty.<br /> <br /> So, 95% of the time, the charm is &quot;Pay 1wp, get +1 specialties on Resistance and Survival&quot;. Considering the charm is 8/10xp, and specialties cost 3xp each (or, hey, you could just buy more Resistance and Survival), I don't think it's worth spending 8/10xp and 1wp a day for a couple of specialties, even if you can apply them to different environments when you feel like it.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest, I've basically bumped up the charms' power by letting the Casteless character not make Resistance rolls for walking around the North in late winter without many clothes on (well, he's got a polar bear cloak now, but he still doesn't wear a shirt), because a)the charm is rubbish, and b)I can't be bothered to punish him for an aesthetic choice.<br /> <br /> I should say that the Protean benefit is okay (not amazing, but possibly you could do something good with Stamina charms) and the repurchase at Essence 2 is good. It's just the base charm that's weak.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Every other charm my players have seems good. It's just this one that seems weak.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I Asked the Devs about this during the KS, and apparently Rugged Beast Endurance should grant the same benefits as Hardship Surviving Mendicant Spirit for areas in which they\u2019ve gained specialties, the charm just neglected to actually say that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-14T10:07:22-07:00","id":1330942,"title":"","content":"Huh, really? That'd make much more sense. Hmmm... do you have a link or something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-14T10:52:30-07:00","id":1330946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330942#post1330942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, really? That'd make much more sense. Hmmm... do you have a link or something?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1297611#post1297611\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1297611#post1297611\"> Ask the Devs v2 - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1297611#post1297611\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1297611#post1297611 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> It seems that, in my hubris, I've let the original Ask the Devs thread get a bit too long. If y'all wouldn't mind posting any new questions here. Thread rules </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1299042#post1299042\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1299042#post1299042\"> Ask the Devs v2 - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1299042#post1299042\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1299042#post1299042 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> It seems that, in my hubris, I've let the original Ask the Devs thread get a bit too long. If y'all wouldn't mind posting any new questions here. Thread rules </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-14T11:18:48-07:00","id":1330949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330914#post1330914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In normal, everyday attire, what penalty would you apply?<br /> <br /> <br /> I expect at least this much strength from a charm: <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=c_1FJGCAPxo\" target=\"_blank\">https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=c_1FJGCAPxo</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I must say I find the Charm cool and I think it's powerful, but it's true in many situations ST would just apply no penalty to do the same thing (or better) because they just wouldn't think of it.<br /> <br /> And it's a problem I encountered wich many Charms : When you read them, you realize &quot;So I actually need a Charm to do this thing I've been doing for the whole campaign ?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-14T12:31:06-07:00","id":1330964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330946#post1330946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1297611#post1297611\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1297611#post1297611\"> Ask the Devs v2 - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1297611#post1297611\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1297611#post1297611 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> It seems that, in my hubris, I've let the original Ask the Devs thread get a bit too long. If y'all wouldn't mind posting any new questions here. Thread rules </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1299042#post1299042\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...42#post1299042</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that's great, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-14T13:18:45-07:00","id":1330975,"title":"","content":"We need a term for air-breathing mermaid where you go &quot;wait, shit, maybe they <i>shouldn't </i> have been able to do that.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-14T14:20:33-07:00","id":1330990,"title":"","content":"Water breathing man?<br /> <br /> Though I think the bigger problems are Charms where there isn't an easy binary of &quot;can/can't&quot; do something.<br /> <br /> With hiding things on your person there's a lot of &quot;depends&quot; on whether or not it should have required a Charm to do. The Pirates of the Caribbean clip above makes sense as not needing a Charm for all but one of those weapons... and since that's basically just a gag in an action comedy could probably be counted as a Stunt rather than a Charm. She's wearing clothing specifically to disguise how well armed she is, and it doesn't even work once she comes under close scrutiny. Hiding all of that in a bikini seem to obviously require a Charm. But how much can you get away with in the middle? Kinda just has to be a ST call on some level.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-14T15:01:06-07:00","id":1330998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330914#post1330914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In normal, everyday attire, what penalty would you apply?</div> </div> </div> </div>To answer this we have to look at what the actual mechanics are for concealing something on your person. You'd think it'd be a contested roll with a penalty for how hard of a thing you're attempting, like disguises are. That doesn't really work though because the Concealable tag sets the difficulty to conceal items at 1, so a difficulty is involved. Since a difficulty is involved, we don't use penalty dice, we use variable difficulty. So just like a disguise check we roll a conceal check against the variable difficulty, if we succeed then the item is concealed, and any threshold successes increase the difficulty to spot it if scrutinized.<br /> <br /> So, for instance, if you're trying to conceal a short sword in a fairly big dress that might be difficulty 2, so you roll it up and get 3 successes. At this point it IS hidden, somebody who sweeps a room won't automatically pick up that you're armed among the crowd like they would if you had it hanging off your belt. If somebody actually takes the time to scrutinize you though, it's not hard for them to spot that shape under your dress and your awkward way of moving. Unless you're a masterful spy who got like 6 successes, in which case only the most perceptive people in the world really stand a chance at seeing it.<br /> <br /> So given that if you're trying to conceal a sword it depends on the situation, and your attire helps a lot. You'd have some at <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/42/ba/e8/42bae83ea2ec18a4855e3ff3f4a88f93.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">difficulty 1</a> or maybe even 0. That dress is big enough for multiple other characters to be able to make stealth checks in your skirt, you could hide a small armory in it. Then you have some at <a href=\"https://images-na.ssl-images-amazon.com/images/I/61Ayix5eCgL._UX522_.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">difficulty 4-5</a>, depending on what you tried to hide and how many. Hiding a short sword in that qipao without being noticed is almost physically impossible, but in the fantasy world of exalted you could try it...but without magic or the greatest roll ever it's not going to stand up to much.<br /> <br /> So then what that said, hiding items with Naked Thief Style allows you to attempt that concealment just straight for a number of items equal to your dexterity.<br /> <br /> <br /> If that isn't the case then the charm the charm does almost nothing. It calls out that you may roll to conceal things on your person, which you clearly can do anyway there's a friggin Concealable tag for weapons which specifically lowers the difficulty, it doesn't enable concealment, and doesn't give any bonus except for being non-contested past medium range. If that was the case the charm should just say &quot;characters can not attempt to spot items concealed on the terrestrial's body from distances greater than Short Range.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330914#post1330914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I expect at least this much strength from a charm: <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=c_1FJGCAPxo\" target=\"_blank\">https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=c_1FJGCAPxo</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Does it...not do that? I think it probably does more actually since in that scene Elizabeth realized the jig was up and disarmed herself, whereas a Terrestrial exalt would just shrug, take off all her outer clothing and say &quot;Yeah? You see any guns here?&quot; and then as soon as a fight breaks out she's got a sword in one hand and throwing bombs with the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-14T15:34:47-07:00","id":1331003,"title":"","content":"[Edit]<br /> <br /> My reading of this Charm was completely wrong as <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1331064#post1331064\">Vance confirms</a>.<br /> <br /> You can ignore everything I've written below:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330990#post1330990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I think the bigger problems are Charms where there isn't an easy binary of &quot;can/can't&quot; do something.<br /> <br /> With hiding things on your person there's a lot of &quot;depends&quot; on whether or not it should have required a Charm to do. The Pirates of the Caribbean clip above makes sense as not needing a Charm for all but one of those weapons... and since that's basically just a gag in an action comedy could probably be counted as a Stunt rather than a Charm. She's wearing clothing specifically to disguise how well armed she is, and it doesn't even work once she comes under close scrutiny. Hiding all of that in a bikini seem to obviously require a Charm. But how much can you get away with in the middle? Kinda just has to be a ST call on some level.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is, the Charm doesn't even work once you're in Short range. Not Close, Short. A spear's throw. At least Elizabeth Swan made it to Close.<br /> <br /> And the idea of hiding thieves' tools in a bikini is a non-starter for me. When would I ever be in a situation where I have thieves' tools to hide but have to wear a bikini? When is that ever going to come up in play? Especially as The Realm explicitly lays out the fashions you're expected to wear and it's not skimpy bikinis.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://keychain.patternspider.net/archive/koc0069.html\" target=\"_blank\">What is an item small enough to hold in one hand?</a><br /> <br /> It's like a Charm that gives you a perfect defence against Boxing Attacks made from Medium range unless the attacker is using Charms, when Boxing Attacks don't exist and couldn't be made from Medium range without Charms anyway.<br /> <br /> And it's a Larceny 3 Charm with a pre-req. And it builds to a Charm that lets you bury things in the ground. And that's it: hiding lockpicks in your clothes or burying them in the ground is the Dragon-Blooded peak for Larceny. Compared to 2E which let them form theives' tools from Essence, or 3E Solars who don't need lockpicks with a Larceny 2/Essence 1 Charm and at Essence 2 can cause 5 small items to disappear from existence until she needs them, not even sending them Elsewhere, untrumpable by magic or simply being close enough to search.<br /> <br /> You can hide small items in your clothing. That doesn't need a Charm. No ST discretion. End of story. The Charm text talks about hiding lockpicks in your hair: that doesn't need <i>two Charms</i> -- even if you are wearing a bikini.<br /> <br /> This is just my opinion, and I realise I'm taking a hard-line on this, but there is no &quot;reasonable middle ground&quot; to be found here. I'd sooner take a Charm that stopped my shoelaces coming untied, or which stopped me accidently swallowing my tongue.<br /> <br /> I have absolutely no interest in playing Exalted with anyone who thinks you need two charms to hide lockpicks in your hair, and the Charm only works with a successful roll, only from Medium range or further away, and is trumped if contested by magic.<br /> <br /> Even hiding a short diaklave in a bikini (something that's not supported by the Charm's text) is of such ridiculously niche use, I couldn't ever justify taking two Charms to do it. (Especially as Elemental Sheath and Invisibly Hidden Chakram Method exist.)<br /> <br /> But, again, just my opinion. I'm not a dev. I'm not anyone remotely important. And by-and-large, I like E3 (and I think Eric and Vance are much better than John and Holden). And if anyone really wants to get into what you can hide without a Charm, that's not &quot;badwrongfun&quot; -- it's just not for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 08-15-2019, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-14T16:01:04-07:00","id":1331006,"title":"","content":"It seems to me that the main point of the charm is to let you conceal small things even when you shouldn't be able to do it. The charm doesn't stop working at short range, it allows a roll to see the concealed items. You could effectively go around naked and conceal small items on your body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12370-lddm84","name":"LDDM84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T01:09:19-07:00","id":1331040,"title":"","content":"[Edit]<br /> <br /> My reading of this Charm was completely wrong as <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1331064#post1331064\">Vance confirms</a>.<br /> <br /> You can ignore everything I've written below:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330998#post1330998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To answer this we have to look at what the actual mechanics are for concealing something on your person. You'd think it'd be a contested roll with a penalty for how hard of a thing you're attempting, like disguises are. That doesn't really work though because the Concealable tag sets the difficulty to conceal items at 1, so a difficulty is involved. Since a difficulty is involved, we don't use penalty dice, we use variable difficulty. So just like a disguise check we roll a conceal check against the variable difficulty, if we succeed then the item is concealed, and any threshold successes increase the difficulty to spot it if scrutinized.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's logical.<br /> <br /> As the Charm is talking about hiding lockpicks in your hair or a set of theives' tools, I don't see the Difficulty being higher than 1.<br /> <br /> The Charm says nothing about lowering the Difficulty of hiding these items on your person.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So given that if you're trying to conceal a sword it depends on the situation, and your attire helps a lot. You'd have some at <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://i.pinimg.com/originals/42/ba/e8/42bae83ea2ec18a4855e3ff3f4a88f93.jpg&quot;]difficulty</a> 1[/URL] or maybe even 0. That dress is big enough for multiple other characters to be able to make stealth checks in your skirt, you could hide a small armory in it. Then you have some at <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://images-na.ssl-images-amazon.com/images/I/61Ayix5eCgL._UX522_.jpg&quot;]difficulty</a> 4-5[/URL], depending on what you tried to hide and how many. Hiding a short sword in that qipao without being noticed is almost physically impossible, but in the fantasy world of exalted you could try it...but without magic or the greatest roll ever it's not going to stand up to much. </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=nwgdgjH0U-U\" target=\"_blank\">5 Dex, 5 Larceny, 2 successes from Underground Rivers Flow, Stunt.</a><br /> <br /> And, again, nothing in this Charm suggests that you can use it to hide swords. Or that it changes the Difficulty of hiding items on your person. (Or that you can hide other characters in your clothes.)<br /> <br /> The Charm allows you to hide &quot;a single item small enough for her to hold in one hand, or an entire set of thieves\u2019 tools&quot; and gives the example of &quot;concealing her lock picks in her coiffure&quot;.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So then what that said, hiding items with Naked Thief Style allows you to attempt that concealment just straight for a number of items equal to your dexterity.<br /> <br /> <br /> If that isn't the case then the charm the charm does almost nothing. It calls out that you may roll to conceal things on your person, which you clearly can do anyway there's a friggin Concealable tag for weapons which specifically lowers the difficulty, it doesn't enable concealment, and doesn't give any bonus except for being non-contested past medium range. If that was the case the charm should just say &quot;characters can not attempt to spot items concealed on the terrestrial's body from distances greater than Short Range.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I don't know what it is you think this Charm does.<br /> <br /> Do you think it sets the Difficulty to hide things on your body to 0? That's still pretty underwhelming but it's significantly better than my reading.<br /> <br /> A short diaklave is <i>significantly</i> bigger than the set of thieves' tools allowed by this Charm. Given what the Charm text allows you to hide, I wouldn't allow weapons which don't have the Concealable tag. Even a normal Knife is pushing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does it...not do that? I think it probably does more actually since in that scene Elizabeth realized the jig was up and disarmed herself, whereas a Terrestrial exalt would just shrug, take off all her outer clothing and say &quot;Yeah? You see any guns here?&quot; and then as soon as a fight breaks out she's got a sword in one hand and throwing bombs with the other. </div> </div> </div>Elizabeth is hiding weapons (not called out as permissible by this Charm), larger than a set of theives' tools, and there's more than five items.<br /> <br /> Let me hide a diaklave, a dozen throwing knives, a brace of flame pieces, a small bomb AND a glass flask of acid and hand winch and we're into Charm territory.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1330801#post1330801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue that the real benefit isn't the range of detection, it's the fact that it seems to allow an unpenalized roll no matter how you're dressed</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are you getting that the roll is unpenalized from?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (handy when you're trying to slip thieves tools in while disguised as an exotic dancer, for instance) </div> </div> </div>Exalted came out in, what, 2001?<br /> <br /> At any point in the last 18 years have you ever played an exotic dancer who needed a set of theives' tools?<br /> <br /> It's never come up in my games. If you say this is useful at your table then I believe you, no contest, please accept my apologies. But as a player or ST, I've never had this come up at my table or on the White Wolf RP Chatroom.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LDDM84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1331006#post1331006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me that the main point of the charm is to let you conceal small things even when you shouldn't be able to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>When shouldn't you be allowed to do it?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You could effectively go around naked and conceal small items on your body. </div> </div> </div>Has that ever come up in play for you?<br /> <br /> Do you think you shouldn't be allowed to hide lockpicks in your hair if you are naked?<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Look, I don't mean to be belligerent about this so I'm going to bow out before I make anyone uncomfortable. I'm just going to Ask the Devs how this works, and I'll link that back to here.<br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> My reading of this Charm was completely wrong: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1331064#post1331064\">link</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 08-15-2019, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T04:19:00-07:00","id":1331050,"title":"","content":"No no, i agree with you. The charm is weak. But what I think it does is a little different of what you think it does. At least, it seems like to be able to conceal little things (something the size of your hand), like a flask, small bomb, small knife or needle, even if you are naked at a flat roll. It still is underwhelming.<br /> <br /> It could be better if the contested roll would be possible only at close range or with magic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12370-lddm84","name":"LDDM84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T06:29:19-07:00","id":1331056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1331040#post1331040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, again, nothing in this Charm suggests that you can use it to hide swords. Or that it changes the Difficulty of hiding items on your person. (Or that you can hide other characters in your clothes.)<br /> <br /> The Charm allows you to hide &amp;quot;a single item small enough for her to hold in one hand, or an entire set of thieves\u2019 tools&amp;quot; and gives the example of &amp;quot;concealing her lock picks in her coiffure&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> I don't know what it is you think this Charm does.<br /> <br /> Do you think it sets the Difficulty to hide things on your body to 0? That's still pretty underwhelming but it's significantly better than my reading.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay but follow me here, if it doesn\u2019t set the difficulty to 0, then what is the difficulty? Is it just the difficulty of hiding a lockpick on your person? Well if that\u2019s the case then what does the charm even do? You\u2019re paying 1m to roll to do something you could do anyway at the same difficulty you could do it at without the charm. I think the only reading of that that makes sense is if all the charm does is prevent contested rolls for medium range and only for the items specifically hidden that way, which would indeed make it a useless charm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1331040#post1331040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elizabeth is hiding weapons (not called out as permissible by this Charm), larger than a set of theives' tools, and there's more than five items.<br /> <br /> Let me hide a diaklave, a dozen throwing knives, a brace of flame pieces, a small bomb AND a glass flask of acid and hand winch and we're into Charm territory.<br /> Where are you getting that the roll is unpenalized from?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m pretty sure even Solars can\u2019t do that, right? Not without wearing an outfit that\u2019s giant and baggy. Proof Eating Palm doesn\u2019t even say \u201can object small enough to hold in one hand.\u201d It says \u201can object small enough to palm.\u201d Which is like a coin, playing card, maybe a small dagger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T07:19:29-07:00","id":1331060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1331056#post1331056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m pretty sure even Solars can\u2019t do that, right? Not without wearing an outfit that\u2019s giant and baggy. Proof Eating Palm doesn\u2019t even say \u201can object small enough to hold in one hand.\u201d It says \u201can object small enough to palm.\u201d Which is like a coin, playing card, maybe a small dagger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars have Many-Pockets Meditation. But sure, Solars don't have such a Charm (but they can send weapons, armor, tack &amp; barding and musical instruments Elsewhere).<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> So what other charms underwhelm people?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T08:04:57-07:00","id":1331066,"title":"","content":"I'm quite surprised by Vance's ruling that you can use Naked Thief to hide a daiklaive, but it does make it a decent charm.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T08:36:45-07:00","id":1331070,"title":"","content":"Automatically making the concealment into an opposed roll also helps. DB excellencies may not go that high, but if you full excellency the concealment, it would take an exalt guard with specialized Charms or who Full Excellencies to spot your daiklave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T08:46:30-07:00","id":1331074,"title":"","content":"So as stated <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1331064#post1331064\">Vance confirms</a> that you can straight up <a href=\"https://keychain.patternspider.net/archive/koc0069.html\" target=\"_blank\">do this</a> with Naked Thief Style.<br /> <br /> Hiding five full sized Diaklaves at difficulty 0 in a bikini and not even letting people try to contest that unless they're at Short range or have magic eyeballs is fair for a two-Charm investment.<br /> <br /> Actually it's pretty good for 1m. I am sufficiently whelmed.<br /> <br /> Compared to, say, Many-Pockets Meditation, I'm not overwhelmed, but I'm not underwhelmed (and I am in Europe).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 08-15-2019, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T09:56:13-07:00","id":1331082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1331066#post1331066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm quite surprised by Vance's ruling that you can use Naked Thief to hide a daiklaive, but it does make it a decent charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the weakest class of charm in the game, Essence 1 DB charm, it\u2019s very good. It\u2019s not quite the Solar one, which doesn\u2019t let you hide things nearly as big, and you get it one Essence later, but it\u2019s also reflexive and doesn\u2019t commit motes, require five dex for five items or allow a contested roll. With how hard the DB contested roll is and being able to conceal Daiklaves it\u2019s not just the Solar one but worse.<br /> <br /> It also occurs to me that it calls out things like disguise kits and thief tools because otherwise the ST might assume you need a mote committed for each lockpick or for the false nose, scarf ect. in the disguise since they consist of multiple items. Same for the \u201cobject hold in one hand.\u201d thing, if it was just an object you\u2019d definitely get a lot of \u201cweeellll technically this trireme is a single object...\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Keeping in theme with the thread though, am I the only one who\u2019s not impressed by almost any charm that involves a distract gambit? Distract is already a gambit that doesn\u2019t see a lot of use, I feel like charms like Elusive Zephyr Strike from Air Thrown or Twin Fang Strike for Lunars? They\u2019re not all bad, With One Mind\u2019s distract effect is dope, and Deadly Wolf Pack Onslaught is...okay but at the Essence you get it at you\u2019re at best making a risky decisive attack and only generating 6i which must be used in a specific way against the same target.<br /> <br /> With the distract gambit already being so useless you\u2019d figure some of the charms could like, add (Essence) to the initiative the beneficiary receives or something. I might be wrong though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T12:41:05-07:00","id":1331100,"title":"","content":"Has anyone mentioned Excellent Friend Method? Thats my go to example of a Charm that strikes me as being really unnecesary. If an NPC already has a Defining Intimacy of loyalty to you that means your one of the central pillars of that persons world. Why would I as the ST demand that asking them to deliver a message, cook you a meal, or whatever other minor task requires a roll in the first place. <br /> <br /> Even if I did demand a roll, just so this charm had some value, it would be of trivial difficulty after the player tapped his Intimacy to lower resolve?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T12:48:49-07:00","id":1331102,"title":"","content":"Might have been a fluke, but we saw a lot of use of Distract. My character in particular was good enough in combat to build up some Initiative (and had a great JB), but didn't have a lot of Decisive boosts. So tossing the Init to our Dawn Tiger MA user to help them get into Form Reflexively on the first round, on our archer to use Blood Without Balance for two Decisives in a row at range, or even just setting up my familiar (based on the eagle stat block) who could get double 10s on decisive damage my character didn't was generally more effectively than nibbling a few HLs off.<br /> <br /> Since we kinda stumbled into it happening to work with the group of characters we made, it's probably not the greatest data point. When we considered building a more Distract oriented character, it got kinda weird since the two main path towards getting better at Distract also open up Charms that make you better at dishing out damage so...who knows. We definitely felt Solar Dodge could have used a combo of a Charm to Distract using Dodge, and Guard-Breaking Technique.<br /> <br /> But that was a Solars game, so I'm not sure how much the DB and Lunar Charms would have interacted in practice. I'd need to compare things to the Solar Thrown gambit boosters to see how I feel in theory.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T13:06:59-07:00","id":1331104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1329866-charms-of-underwhelming-might?p=1331100#post1331100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would I as the ST demand that asking them to deliver a message, cook you a meal, or whatever other minor task requires a roll in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>It works on inconvenient tasks, not just trivial ones. You're still asking them to do something they wouldn't do on their own because they trust you, even if not ones with terribly high risks involved.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even if I did demand a roll, just so this charm had some value, it would be of trivial difficulty after the player tapped his Intimacy to lower resolve? </div> </div> </div>Consider that characters can have multiple Intimacies in all this. If you're trying to Persuade someone to do something using your Defining Intimacy that opposes one of their Major Intimacies, it's a wash on the bonuses/penalties. So it's as difficult as their Resolve naturally is. This isn't for getting your servants to do stuff, it's for getting a Terrestrial that you've bonded with in the heat of battle fighting something obviously evil so they're now conflicted with strong ties to you as both an Anathema but a clear warrior for good, and the teachings the Immaculates and duties to the Realm they haven't shaken off yet.<br /> <br /> Plus Excellent Friend Approach is a permanent Charm. It's not like it costs you anything to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}